{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/781823-remembering-arcadia-homebrew","id":781823,"title":"Remembering Arcadia (Homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-07T13:41:25-08:00","id":781823,"title":"Remembering Arcadia (Homebrew)","content":"So, this is my first shot at writing anything for Changeling. It's probably not accurate by any stretch of the imagination, but I kind of threw together some mechanics on when/how a Changeling dreams of Arcadia and their Durance, and how much they remember. I sort of retrofitted Mummy's Memory system to work for this, but in reverse to its usual order. High-Clarity Changeling is the equivalent of a Low-Memory Mummy in terms of what they remember of Faerie. Lets them run off and be human, but leaves them a bit more vulnerable to the machinations of Faerie. As the Changeling's Clarity falls, they begin to remember Arcadia in more accurate and vivid ways, even gaining Merits at low levels the way Mummies gain Merits at high levels.<br /> <br /> The general idea was, fresh out of the Thorns, a Changeling would try to go home and the major changes that occurred would cause a hurricane of Clarity Breaking Points early on, dropping them fairly quickly from Clarity 10 to Clarity 7, at which point they would probably try and find other Changelings, or their existential crisis and ramblings about Arcadia and faeries would lead to them being found by the local Freehold.<br /> <br /> Any feedback is good feedback, and I totally expect to be ripped apart by the extremely loyal fans of <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>, but if you have any suggestions for improvement, that would be great.<br /> <br /> <b>Remembering Arcadia: </b>Most Changelings would be quite happy if they could live their lives pretending Arcadia didn\u2019t exist, that they weren\u2019t subjected to their Durance, and that they haven\u2019t lost significant portions of their lives at the hands of the True Fae. Sacrificing the portion of yourself to make a space for your Seeming, and having bits torn to pieces by the thorns of the Hedge and the power of the Wyrd, means memories can be threadbare at best, and terrifyingly vivid at worst. And no matter how deeply the horror is buried, it always finds a way back to the surface.<br /> <br /> When your Changeling sleeps, roll their Wyrd. If the roll is successful, they dream of Arcadia and their Durance. What, and how much, they remember is dictated by their Clarity. If the Intensity of the dream is equal to or greater than their Clarity, they suffer a Breaking Point and do not gain Willpower from sleep.<br /> <br /> A Changeling at Clarity 0 is a terrifying thing, closer to True Fae than to a human being, they behave almost entirely according to the Wyrd, following their own story, reliving and reenacting their own Durance in horrible, nightmarish ways. It is possible to bring them back from the brink, however, with intensive oneiromancy that restores their sense of self and a grip on reality. Another Changeling must Scour the Intensity of their dreams for a number of days equal to the Clarity 0 Changeling\u2019s Wyrd, then perform Psychotherapy for a number of days equal to the Changeling\u2019s Wyrd, in order to restore them to Clarity 1. From there, it is best to keep them isolated and acting in accord with their Seeming until they have recovered. Certain Contracts, entering deep parts of the Hedge, and direct contact with their own Keeper may temporarily drop a Changeling to Clarity 0. After that, they will be unable to remember such loses of reality at Clarity 4 and above.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Clarity</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>What They Remember of Faerie</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">They remember snippets of their Durance and aspects of their fae life. At this level, the Changeling has an incredibly strong grasp on reality and attempts to avoid anything to do with Faerie. They can almost convince themselves that they are human, even if their reflection may say otherwise.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Remembers their alias, their escape, and some fae lore. They may invent a delusional history for themselves, but they know they need to stay hidden.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">They remember their fae alias, the fact they were taken to Arcadia, and their escape. They have trouble distinguishing between personal experience, lessons, and stories in terms of fae lore and magic.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">At this level, they remember one significant part of their Durance. They remember suffering in Arcadia, their escape, and their Keeper, but in a more surreal fashion.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">They remember a major event from their Durance in great detail, with rough knowledge of the rest of their time in Arcadia as well. This is the highest rank at which they remember their capture and escape with any kind of real completion- how they were taken to Arcadia, what convinced them to escape, and the choice they made that enabled them to get away.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">The Changeling accurately recalls two major events of their Durance. One that carries the weight of the Wyrd (narrative importance) and one with great emotional significance. While other parts of the Durance are fragmentary and hazy, they can recognize other Changelings they were imprisoned with.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">They remember every part of their Durance in the broad strokes</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">The highest rank at which they remember Arcadia with any kind of reliability. They also remember, (possibly to their horror), anything they did while temporarily at Clarity 0.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">They recall Arcadia and their Durance in remarkable detail, giving them surer footing in the Hedge and even Arcadia itself than they normally would. They\u2019ve followed the Trods many times before. While in the Hedge or Arcadia, the Changeling gains the Direction Sense merit for free, and may purchase the Advanced or Epic version of the merit, even though they aren\u2019t a Beast.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">The Changeling remembers nearly everything about their Durance, and sees the strands of the Wyrd and the flow of Glamour in everything. They gain the Unseen Sense: Wyrd merit for free. This enables them to sense what follows or disrupts Fate, as well as to sense when anyone calls upon the Wyrd, enabling them to detect Pledges, Talecrafting, Goblin Vows, and other acts of magic that use the Wyrd directly instead of Glamour. If they gain Clarity, they lose access to the merit.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">The Changeling remembers their Durance in perfect clarity to the point that some will continue to act as though still in Arcadia or evading capture. They follow Pledges to the letter, if not the spirit, and attempt to follow the Wyrd in everything they do, acting more along the lines of narrative than their own will.</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T18:51:48-08:00","id":782005,"title":"","content":"So, before I respond substantively, I have to ask: why? What's the purpose of this? What are you trying to achieve? Are you trying to play Mummy using Changeling powers, for instance? (That would be an interesting approach to playing a Wolverine expy, incidentally.) Are you trying to create benefits for having low Clarity? Are you trying to create a more espionage-y feel to high Clarity play? Do you find Clarity overly boring and want to spice it up in general?<br /> <br /> What's the goal here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T19:28:41-08:00","id":782025,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to spice up Clarity a bit. The fluff describes low - Clarity as a slide into a mindset similar to the True Fae, given to seeing fantastic things in everyday life, and in general losing their grip on reality. More importantly, it also at times describes memories and dreams of Arcadia as fragmentary and unreliable. <br /> <br /> I figured I'd mix the two together, and tie awareness and remembrance of Faerie with less of a grip on the real world, as well as some 'benefits' to low Clarity. It's still in the design process, but the general idea is that the dubious sanity of low Clarity (as represented by Conditions gained through Breaking Points) is tempting. Some might want to remember, others might be lured by potential power. (I'm planning on adding some benefits to certain Contracts and other abilities) The idea being that Faerie is seductive, and so giving in to it should be tempting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T01:10:38-08:00","id":782677,"title":"","content":"You should give a Clarity 1-3 things to make them reason that Arcadia is &quot;more real&quot; than real life, somehow. Maybe indulging in their day dreaming gives them Willpower back, as extra means? Or that they see <b>all</b> supernatural phenomena, in the Arcadia way. Low Clairy changeling can see things that other cannot see. Only real life to them sounds more and more like a dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}